BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Michael Mann’s Manhunter: The Final Cut with Michael Mann
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260612
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260613
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd53d-50af-baad-9b14-3838732fe7b0@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: writer and director Michael Mann\n\nFriday\, June 1
 2\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h\n\n
 1986 | 120 min. | USA | Color | Scope | English | Rated R | 4K DCP \nDIREC
 TED/WRITTEN BY: Michael Mann \nWITH: William Petersen\, Kim Greist\, Joan 
 Allen\, Tom Noonan\n\nType: Screenings\n\nA retired criminal profiler (Wil
 liam Petersen) reluctantly returns to the FBI to help track down a serial 
 killer of families and is forced to consult an expert—the imprisoned Dr.
  Hannibal Lecktor (Brian Cox in a subtly chilling performance). The third 
 feature written and directed by Michael Mann is a gripping adaptation of t
 he first of Thomas Harris’s four novels featuring the iconic murderer\, 
 and benefits from the filmmaker’s typically striking visuals as well as 
 a top-notch supporting cast\, including Tom Noonan as the hunted killer\, 
 and three-time Oscar nominee Joan Allen (The Contender\, 2000) as his blin
 d love interest.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/manhunter-the-final-c
 ut-with-michael-mann-019dd53d-50af-baad-9b14-3838732fe7b0
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Gentlemen Prefer Blondes with Monkey Business in 4K
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260612
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260613
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dda5a-ab50-7efe-4f00-64859f98521f@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, June 12\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 31m\n\n1953 | 91 min. | USA | Technicolor | Englis
 h | Not Rated | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Howard Hawks  \nWRITTEN BY: Charles L
 ederer  \nWITH: Jane Russell\, Marilyn Monroe\, Charles Coburn\, Elliott 
 Reid\n\nType: Screenings\n\nGentlemen Prefer Blondes In this 1953 musical 
 comedy\, adapted from Joseph Fields and Anita Loos’s searingly funny sta
 ge musical based on her 1925 novella\, showgirl Lorelei (Marilyn Monroe) i
 s resplendent in beautiful gowns\, most notably in the pink satin dress de
 signed by Travilla during the now-classic number “Diamonds Are a Girl’
 s Best Friend.” Lorelei is seen throughout the picture in jewel tones an
 d literal jewels\, carefully selected to play up the lush Technicolor cine
 matography lensed by Harry J. Wild. Both effervescent and timeless\, this 
 witty gem showcases Monroe’s brilliant comic timing as well as her vocal
  chops. Premiering in the middle of the actress’s career and released th
 e same year as Niagara and How to Marry a Millionaire\, Howard Hawks’s f
 ilm helped to plant Monroe in the hearts of the American public\, making h
 er one of the most famous people in the US.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/gentlemen-prefer-blon
 des-with-monkey-business-019dda5a-ab50-7efe-4f00-64859f98521f
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Grave of the Fireflies
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260612
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260613
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd4e4-37b6-8f02-4401-b45c3e697267@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, June 12\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 29m\n\n1988 | 89 min. | Japan | Color | Japanese w
 ith English subtitles | Not Rated | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Isao Takahat
 a \nWITH: Tsutomu Tatsumi\, Ayano Shiraishi\, Yoshiko Shinohara\, Akemi Y
 amaguchi\n\nType: Screenings\n\nDirector Isao Takahata’s first film for 
 Studio Ghibli is a harrowing depiction of the last days of World War II as
  seen through the eyes of teenager Seita and his little sister Setsuko. Af
 ter Allied firebombing destroys their home\, family\, and much of Kobe cit
 y\, the two must fend for themselves and search for joy in their war-torn 
 community. Based on Nosaka Akiyuki’s semi-autobiographical account of th
 e same name\, Grave of the Fireflies is an uncompromising portrait of pers
 onal tragedy and loss of innocence in war.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/grave-of-the-fireflie
 s-019dd4e4-37b6-8f02-4401-b45c3e697267
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bound
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260613
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260614
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd53f-4f70-3abb-8859-66300caa3899@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, June 13\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motio
 n Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 45m\n\n1996 | 105 min. | USA | Color | English |
  Rated R | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: The Wachowskis\nWITH: Jennifer Tilly\
 , Gina Gershon\, Joe Pantoliano\, John P. Ryan\n\nType: Screenings\n\nFres
 h out of prison and wanting to lay low\, Corky (Gina Gershon)\, takes a jo
 b fixing up an old apartment only to be seduced by Violet (Jennifer Tilly)
 \, the high-femme girl next door. As their secret affair heats up\, they d
 evise a plan to steal $2 million from Violet’s mobster boyfriend. In the
  Wachowskis’ feature-film directorial debut\, they subvert traditional g
 ender roles and genre convention\, allowing Corky and Violet to be deeply 
 human as they navigate the boxes society creates for them and take down th
 e oppressive men in their lives. After the Wachowskis refused studio sugge
 stions of changing Corky to a man\, they secured financing from Dino De La
 urentiis\, who supported their original vision and added feminist writer S
 usie Bright as a lesbian sex consultant to create what has now become a cu
 lt classic in queer cinema.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/bound-019dd53f-4f70-3
 abb-8859-66300caa3899
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ladies of the Chorus in 35mm
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260613
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260614
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dda5e-977f-fb03-d37f-5861011de57b@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, June 13\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motio
 n Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 1m\n\n1948 | 61 min | USA | Black-and-White | En
 glish | Not Rated | 35mm \nDIRECTED BY: Phil Karlson \nWRITTEN BY: Harry
  Sauber\, Joseph Carole \nWITH: Marilyn Monroe\, Adele Jergens\, Rand Bro
 oks\, Nana Bryant\n\nType: Screenings\n\nPeggy Martin (Marilyn Monroe)\, a
  burlesque-show chorus girl who works alongside her mother\, Mae (Adele Je
 rgens)\, gets her big break after the lead unexpectedly quits. When Peggy 
 is pursued by the wealthy society man\, Randy Carroll (Rand Brooks)\, Mae 
 worries their class differences will doom the relationship and tries to pr
 otect Peggy from the same heartbreak she once suffered. Ladies of the Chor
 us features Marilyn’s first starring role\, and her only film role durin
 g her short stint on contract at Columbia Pictures. The film also marked t
 he first time Monroe sang and danced in a film.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/ladies-of-the-chorus-
 019dda5e-977f-fb03-d37f-5861011de57b
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:How to Marry a Millionaire
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260613
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260614
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dda67-f97f-c6c8-221a-626c11fa6abd@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, June 13\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motio
 n Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 35m\n\n1953 | 95 min | USA | Technicolor | Engli
 sh | Not Rated | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Jean Negulesco \nWRITTEN BY: Nunnall
 y Johnson \nWITH: Betty Grable\, Marilyn Monroe\, Lauren Bacall\, David W
 ayne\n\nType: Screenings\n\nSchatze\, Pola\, and Loco (Lauren Bacall\, Mar
 ilyn Monroe\, Betty Grable) are Manhattan models on a mission to marry ric
 h husbands. Although they set their sights on Vanderbilts and Rockefellers
 \, their plans go awry when they become attracted to men who look to be pe
 nniless. How to Marry a Millionaire was released at the end of Monroe’s 
 breakout year\, having starred in Gentlemen Prefer Blondes and Niagara in 
 1953. The film is notable as the first to be completed in CinemaScope\, an
 d Monroe had such broad appeal that 20th Century-Fox used her to advertise
  this new widescreen format: a slogan above an image of Marilyn claimed sh
 e was “Big as life and a million times more fun in Cinemascope!”
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/how-to-marry-a-millio
 naire-019dda67-f97f-c6c8-221a-626c11fa6abd
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Escape to Witch Mountain
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260613
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260614
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019db0ff-6d56-f857-758e-f7b7876d325b@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, June 13\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motio
 n Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 37m\n\n1975 | 97 min. | USA | Color | English | 
 Rated G | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: John Hough \nWRTTEN BY: Robert Malcolm Young 
 \nWITH: Eddie Albert\, Ray Milland\, Donald Pleasence\, Kim Richards\n\nTy
 pe: Screenings\n\nDisney produced this initial chapter of its Witch Mounta
 in series during its Dark Age. It follows two orphaned siblings\, Tony and
  Tia\, who possess mysterious psychic powers\; Tony can move objects with 
 his harmonica\, while Tia can communicate telepathically and manifest prem
 onition. When the evil\, wealthy Aristotle Bolt\, and his employee\, Lucas
  Deranian\, learn about these enigmatic traits\, they plan a wicked scheme
  to kidnap the siblings. Against the lush greenery of valleys and beautifu
 l ocean\, Tony and Tia’s dangerous escape from Bolt turns into a charmin
 g\, endearing adventure when Jason O’Day\, a widower camper\, joins them
  in search of a place indicated on a map hidden in Tia’s star case\, an 
 item she carries with her at all times.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/escape-to-witch-mount
 ain-019db0ff-6d56-f857-758e-f7b7876d325b
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Offside in 35mm
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260614
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260615
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019de537-5c7e-d4ab-fcac-842733f8eb3d@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, June 14\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 33m\n\n2006 | 93 min. | Iran | Color | Persian | R
 ated PG | 35mm.  \nDIRECTED BY: Jafar Panahi \nWRITTEN BY: Jafar Panahi\
 , Shadmehr Rastin \nWITH: Sima Mobarak Shahi\, Safar Samandar\, Shayesteh
  Irani\, M. Kheyrabadi\n\nType: Screenings\n\nSince 1979\, women in Iran h
 ave been barred from attending male sporting events\, though intrepid fema
 le fans often disguise themselves as men to gain access. After his daughte
 r tried the same on multiple occasions\, filmmaker Jafar Panahi co-wrote t
 his narrativized account of young women who attempt to sneak into the June
  2005 Iran/Bahrain FIFA World Cup-qualifying match in Tehran. Oscar-nomina
 ted screenwriter Panahi uses the backdrop of the actual 2005 game to under
 score the overwhelming male presence in public spaces and the inequality f
 aced by women in 2006—a reality still pervasive 20 years later—as well
  as the value of community solidarity in the face of oppressive regulation
 s on the populace.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/offside-019de537-5c7e
 -d4ab-fcac-842733f8eb3d
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shaolin Soccer in 35mm
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260614
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260615
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019de536-3069-56db-33cf-a0f9f32f6717@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, June 14\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 27m\n\n2001 | 87 min. | Hong Kong | Color | Englis
 h dubbed | Rated PG-13 | 35mm \nDIRECTED BY: Stephen Chow \nWRITTEN BY: S
 tephen Chow\, Tsang Kan-cheung \nWITH: Stephen Chow\, Vicki Zhao\, Ng Man
 -tat\, Wong Yat-fei \n35mm print courtesy of Paramount Pictures Archive.\n
 \nType: Screenings\n\nSing (Stephen Chow)\, a former Shaolin monk known as
  Mighty Steel Leg\, is down on his luck. Poor and unable to recruit studen
 ts to carry out his dream of popularizing martial arts in the modern world
 \, he resorts to petty theft to survive. When former soccer player Golden 
 Leg Fung (longtime Chow collaborator Ng Man-tat) whose dreams of stardom w
 ere squashed years prior\, notices Sing’s superhuman abilities\, he pers
 uades him to use his skills for soccer. Sing assembles a team of martial-a
 rts masters to face off against a colorful swath of eccentric professional
  players. Stephen Chow’s slapstick sports comedy was a smash hit in Hong
  Kong and introduced Chow’s signature style to an international audience
 .
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/shaolin-soccer-019de5
 36-3069-56db-33cf-a0f9f32f6717
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bend It Like Beckham in 35mm
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260614
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260615
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019de534-a9ce-c7f9-7cea-8357cbbf429a@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, June 14\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 52m\n\n2002 | 112 min. | UK/Germany/USA | Color | 
 English | Rated PG-13 | 35mm  \nDIRECTED BY: Gurinder Chadha \nWRITTEN B
 Y: Gurinder Chadha\, Guljit Bindra\, Paul Mayeda Berges \nWITH: Parminder
  Nagra\, Keira Knightley\, Jonathan Rhys Meyers\, Anupam Kher\n\nType: Scr
 eenings\n\nJesminder “Jess” Bhamra (Parminder Nagra) dreams of playing
  professional soccer\, but her strict Sikh parents have designs on her fut
 ure as a lawyer and wife. So when Jess is recruited to join the local amat
 eur team by the confident Jules (Keira Knightley)\, Jess keeps the hobby f
 rom her family\, until a publicized match forces her father to reckon with
  his daughter’s true passion. Named for a kick technique popularized by 
 English soccer star David Beckham\, this British comedy was a critical suc
 cess that inspired a generation of women to take up the sport.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/bend-it-like-beckham-
 019de534-a9ce-c7f9-7cea-8357cbbf429a
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The French Connection in 35mm
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260615
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260616
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd56e-ab06-c1c3-3efe-ab5004739894@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, June 15\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 44m\n\n1971 | 104 min. | USA | Color | English | R
 ated R | 35mm \nDIRECTOR: William Friedkin \nWRITTEN BY: Ernest Tidyman 
  \nWITH: Gene Hackman\, Fernando Rey\, Roy Scheider\, Tony Lo Bianco \nP
 rint courtesy of the Academy Film Archive.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nDirector
  William Friedkin helped usher in a new era of gritty police dramas with t
 his fact-based thriller about an unscrupulous New York cop (Gene Hackman\,
  in a star-making\, Best Actor-winning performance) and his sidekick (Roy 
 Scheider) who face an international drug ring. A winner of five Oscars\, i
 ncluding Best Picture and Directing\, The French Connection set a high bar
  for documentary-inspired realism in commercial cinema while featuring one
  of the most exciting car-chase scenes of all time.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-french-connection
 -019dd56e-ab06-c1c3-3efe-ab5004739894
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Only Yesterday
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260615
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260616
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd4e5-382b-1b21-6b82-7f190efce69f@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, June 15\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 58m\n\n1991 | 118 min. | Japan | Color | Japanese 
 with English subtitles | Rated PG | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Isao Takahat
 a \nWITH: Miki Imai\, Toshiro Yanagiba\, Yoko Honna\, Michie Terada\n\nTy
 pe: Screenings\n\nBased on the manga of the same name\, Isao Takahata’s 
 second feature for Studio Ghibli is a serene memory piece featuring 27-yea
 r-old Taeko reminiscing about her 1960s childhood\, travelling from Tokyo 
 to the sleepy country town of Yamagata and rediscovering herself in the pr
 ocess. Takahata renders these flashbacks in a style different from the pre
 sent-day scenes—corners slightly fade into white\, edges blur—lending 
 these moments a sense of impermanence. Though most Japanese anime projects
  record dialogue after animation is finished\, this film reversed much of 
 that process\, allowing the visual artists to create more realistic facial
  expressions. A surprise smash hit in Japan\, the film attracted a largely
  adult audience with its poignant look at the cost of growing up.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/only-yesterday-019dd4
 e5-382b-1b21-6b82-7f190efce69f
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Aardman Animations Celebration
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260617
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260618
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd528-36b1-73cb-59ef-39c58d050ebc@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: animator/filmmaker Bob Persichetti and Academy Gove
 rnors Jinko Gotoh and Marlon West \nSelected by the Animation Branch\n\nWe
 dnesday\, June 17\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\
 nRuntime: 1m\n\nAard Man \n1972 | 1 min | UK | Color | English \nDIRECTED 
 BY: Peter Lord\, David Sproxton \n\nCreature Comforts\n1990 | 5 min. | UK 
 | Color | English \nDIRECTED BY: Nick Park \nWITH: Julie Sedgewick \n\nIde
 nt \n1990 | 5 min. | UK | Color | English \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Richard S
 tarzak \nWITH: Arthur Smith\, Phil Nice \n\nAdam  \n1992 | 6 min. | UK | 
 Color | English \nDIRECTED BY: Peter Lord \nWITH: Nick Upton \n\nThe Wrong
  Trousers \n1993 | 30 min. | UK | Color | English \nDIRECTED BY: Nick Park
  \nWRITTEN BY: Nick Park\, Bob Baker\, Brian Sibley \nWITH: Peter Sallis \
 n\nHumdrum \n1999 | 7 min. | UK | Color | English \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: P
 eter Peake \nWITH: Moray Hunter\, Jack Docherty \n\nOff Beat \n2006 | 3 mi
 n. | UK | Color | English\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Will Becher \nWITH: Michae
 l Buerk \n\nRobin Robin \n2021 | 32 min. | UK | Color | English\nDIRECTED 
 BY: Dan Ojari\, Mikey Please \nWRITTEN BY: Dan Ojari\, Mikey Please\, Sam 
 Morrison \nWITH: Bronte Carmichael\, Richard E. Grant\, Gillian Anderson\,
  Adeel Akhtar\n\nType: Screenings\n\nA selection of short films in celebra
 tion of the internationally acclaimed studio Aardman Animations. Aard Man 
 was the first animated short (25 seconds long) produced by the studio. Cre
 ature Comforts (1990 Animated Short Film winner) puts the voices and words
  of ordinary Brits into the mouths of zoo animals. Ident (1990) tells the 
 story of a clay-man and his changing relationship with the world around hi
 m. Adam (1992 Animated Short Film nominee) takes an unusual look at the Bi
 blical first man. The Wrong Trousers (1993 Animated Short Film winner) pit
 s Wallace and Gromit against a conniving penguin. Humdrum (1993 Animated S
 hort Film nominee) spotlights two bored silhouettes desperately looking fo
 r a way to liven up their day. In Off Beat\, a man takes the opportunity o
 f a police holiday to attempt a crime. Robin Robin (2021 Animated Short no
 minee) tells of a bird raised by mice.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/aardman-animations-50
 th-anniversary-019dd528-36b1-73cb-59ef-39c58d050ebc
END:VEVENT
