 on Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 58m\n\n1991 | 118 min. | Japan | Color | Japane
 se with English subtitles | Rated PG | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Isao Taka
 hata \nWITH: Miki Imai\, Toshiro Yanagiba\, Yoko Honna\, Michie Terada\n\
 nType: Screenings\n\nBased on the manga of the same name\, Isao Takahata
 ’s second feature for Studio Ghibli is a serene memory piece featuring 2
 7-year-old Taeko reminiscing about her 1960s childhood\, travelling from T
 okyo to the sleepy country town of Yamagata and rediscovering herself in t
 he process. Takahata renders these flashbacks in a style different from th
 e present-day scenes—corners slightly fade into white\, edges blur—len
 ding these moments a sense of impermanence. Though most Japanese anime pro
 jects record dialogue after animation is finished\, this film reversed muc
 h of that process\, allowing the visual artists to create more realistic f
 acial expressions. A surprise smash hit in Japan\, the film attracted a la
 rgely adult audience with its poignant look at the cost of growing up.
