BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:10th Anniversary of Spa Night
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260618
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260619
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019de537-df5c-2aca-648c-405bd5af20d1@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: writer/director Andrew Ahn and actor Joe Seo. Moder
 ated by comedian and actor Margaret Cho.\n\nThursday\, June 18\, 2026\n\nL
 ocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 33m\n\n2016 | 93
  min | USA | Color | Korean\, English\, Spanish | Unrated | DCP  \nDIRECT
 ED/WRITTEN BY: Andrew Ahn \nWITH: Joe Seo\, Haerry Kim\, Youn Ho Cho\, Ta
 e Song\n\nType: Screenings\n\nAfter high-school senior David Cho (Joe Seo)
  and his parents\, Soyoung and Jin (Haerry Kim\, Youn-Ho Cho)\, are forced
  to sell their family restaurant\, they take on odd jobs to get by. When h
 is parents enroll David in expensive college prep courses\, he secretly ta
 kes a part-time job at a men’s jjimjilbang (bathhouse) to help with fami
 ly finances. The choice also leads to an unexpected awakening\, allowing D
 avid to explore his sexuality in a space reserved for illicit encounters. 
 \nFilmmaker Andrew Ahn draws from his Korean American upbringing in the bu
 stling Los Angeles neighborhood of Koreatown to capture a story about fami
 lial bonds and expectations\, exploring the intersection of queer and cult
 ural identity within the ongoing pursuit of the so-called American dream.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/spa-night-019de537-df
 5c-2aca-648c-405bd5af20d1
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Parallax View
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260619
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260620
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd571-1467-4501-b84c-022e55e2b969@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, June 19\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 43m\n\n1974 | 103 min. | USA | Color | Scope | Eng
 lish | Rated R | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Alan J. Pakula \nWRITTEN BY: David Gil
 er\, Lorenzo Semple Jr. \nWITH: Warren Beatty\, Hume Cronyn\, William Dani
 els\, Paula Prentiss\n\nType: Screenings\n\nA witness to a political assas
 sination on Seattle’s Space Needle asks investigative journalist Joe Fra
 dy (Warren Beatty) to help protect her\, but the reporter soon finds himse
 lf endangered by vast and terrifying conspiracy. The second film in direct
 or Alan J. Pakula’s unofficial paranoia trilogy (following Klute\, 1971 
 and preceding All the President’s Men\, 1976) is a classic of 1970s susp
 ense cinema\, aided greatly by Michael Small’s unsettling score and the 
 meticulous widescreen cinematography of Gordon Willis (The Godfather\, 197
 2).
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-parallax-view-019
 dd571-1467-4501-b84c-022e55e2b969
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Seven Year Itch with Kim Morgan
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260619
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260620
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dda68-95b6-c5ab-574b-a0563b47ceff@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: writer Kim Morgan\n\nFriday\, June 19\, 2026\n\nLoc
 ation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 45m\n\n1955 | 105 
 min | USA | Color | English | Not Rated | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Billy Wilder
  \nWRITTEN BY: Billy Wilder\, George Axelrod \nWITH: Marilyn Monroe\, To
 mmy Ewell\, Evelyn Keyes\, Sonny Tufts\n\nType: Screenings\n\nOne of Monro
 e’s most successful roles was as The Girl in director Billy Wilder’s T
 he Seven Year Itch\, a comedy about a restless husband left to his own dev
 ices for the summer. To market the film\, photographer Sam Shaw proposed t
 he indelible subway grate moment\, which dozens of publicity photographers
  attended on location in New York City. Due to sound issues\, the real sce
 ne was shot on the 20th Century-Fox lot in Los Angeles. Outside of this ic
 onic scene\, the exhibition Marilyn Monroe: Hollywood Icon also features s
 ilk pajamas worn during a pivotal moment in developing Monroe’s girl-nex
 t-door character.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-seven-year-itch-0
 19dda68-95b6-c5ab-574b-a0563b47ceff
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Only Yesterday
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260619
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260620
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd4e5-e477-ad4a-420b-800337a5ef96@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, June 19\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 58m\n\n1991 | 118 min. | Japan | Color | Japanese 
 with English subtitles | Rated PG | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Isao Takahat
 a \nWITH: Miki Imai\, Toshiro Yanagiba\, Yoko Honna\, Michie Terada\n\nTy
 pe: Screenings\n\nBased on the manga of the same name\, Isao Takahata’s 
 second feature for Studio Ghibli is a serene memory piece featuring 27-yea
 r-old Taeko reminiscing about her 1960s childhood\, travelling from Tokyo 
 to the sleepy country town of Yamagata and rediscovering herself in the pr
 ocess. Takahata renders these flashbacks in a style different from the pre
 sent-day scenes—corners slightly fade into white\, edges blur—lending 
 these moments a sense of impermanence. Though most Japanese anime projects
  record dialogue after animation is finished\, this film reversed much of 
 that process\, allowing the visual artists to create more realistic facial
  expressions. A surprise smash hit in Japan\, the film attracted a largely
  adult audience with its poignant look at the cost of growing up.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/only-yesterday-019dd4
 e5-e477-ad4a-420b-800337a5ef96
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Car Wash 50th Anniversary Screening in 4K
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260620
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260621
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019db106-4226-a625-5d8f-1f850e40e197@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Restoration world premiere \nIn person: filmmaker Michael Schu
 ltz\; actors Bill Duke\, Antonio Fargas\, Melanie Mayron\, Garrett Morris\
 , Pepe Serna. Moderated by Jacqueline Stewart.\n\nSaturday\, June 20\, 202
 6\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 37m\n\n197
 6. 97 min. USA. Color. English. Rated PG. 4K DCP.  \nDIRECTED BY: Michael
  Schultz \nWRITTEN BY: Joel Schumacher  \nWITH: Franklyn Ajaye\, Sully B
 oyar\, Richard Brestoff\, George Carlin\n\nType: Screenings\n\nThe employe
 es of Dee-Luxe Car Wash in Los Angeles are just trying to get through anot
 her workday. Whether it's fending off skater punks\, practicing for an aud
 ition\, or trying to land a date\, the diverse ensemble of Michael Schultz
 ’s effervescent Car Wash approaches its buffing and drying with the yout
 hful energy of an endless summer.\nStacked with Black comedy and cinema lu
 minaries Franklyn Ajaye\, Bill Duke\, Ivan Dixon\, Antonio Fargas\, Garret
 t Morris\, and Richard Pryor\, and supported by George Carlin\, Irwin Core
 y\, and Melanie Mayron\, this who’s-who of 1970s independent and undergr
 ound cinema makes for a joyous slice of life. Underscored by the funky tun
 es of Rose Royce and complemented by a cameo by the Pointer Sisters\, Schu
 ltz’s classic is a witty\, primarily light-hearted offering from an othe
 rwise tumultuous decade. \nSpecial thanks to Kim Taylor-Coleman and Univer
 sal.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/car-wash-50th-anniver
 sary-and-restoration-premiere-019db106-4226-a625-5d8f-1f850e40e197
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:River of No Return
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260620
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260621
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dda5f-18da-8f07-df02-1ca531ee7455@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, June 20\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motio
 n Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 31m\n\n1954 | 91 min | USA | Technicolor | Engli
 sh | Not Rated | DCP\nDIRECTED BY: Otto Preminger \nWRITTEN BY: Frank Fen
 ton \nWITH: Robert Mitchum\, Marilyn Monroe\, Rory Calhoun\, Tommy Rettig
 \n\nType: Screenings\n\nMarilyn Monroe’s appearance in Western genre fil
 ms required designer Travilla to create costumes ranging from saloon-style
  gowns to casual denim looks. Monroe wanted her character\, Kay—a kind-h
 earted saloon singer torn between an ex-convict (Robert Mitchum) and her t
 roubled fiancé (Rory Calhoun)—to have a natural feel. Her acting coach\
 , Natasha Lytess\, and director Otto Preminger clashed over whether Monroe
  should use her typical breathy voice\, with the studio backing Monroe’s
  decision to forgo it.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/river-of-no-return-01
 9dda5f-18da-8f07-df02-1ca531ee7455
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Rescuers
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260620
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260621
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019db100-4895-ac0b-21ed-07abc0c67798@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, June 20\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motio
 n Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 18m\n\n1977 | 78 min. | USA | Color | English | 
 Rated G | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Wolfgang Reitherman\, John Lounsbery\, Art St
 evens \nWRITTEN BY: Larry Clemmons\, Ken Anderson\, Vance Gerry\, Ted Berm
 an\, Burny Mattinson\, Frank Thomas\, David Michener\, Fred Lucky\, Dick S
 ebast \nWITH: Bob Newhart\, Eva Gabor\, Geraldine Page\, Joe Flynn\n\nType
 : Screenings\n\nThe Rescue Aid Society\, an international secret associati
 on of mice\, receives a message in a bottle from an orphaned girl\, Penny\
 , who has been abducted by a pair of treasure collectors\, Madame Medusa a
 nd her partner\, Mr. Snoops. Society members Miss Bianca (Eva Gabor) and B
 ernard (Bob Newhart) begin a rescue journey in search of Penny. Disney’s
  last animated feature processed in Technicolor\, this sweet detective adv
 enture\, nominated for Original Song at the Academy Awards\, showcases a n
 ostalgic ambience drawn from its distinctive color palette\, which harmoni
 zes wonderfully with the film’s dreamlike visual presentation and storyl
 ine\, and its warm performances by Gabor and Newhart.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-rescuers-019db100
 -4895-ac0b-21ed-07abc0c67798
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Summertime in 35mm
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260621
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260622
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019db108-13ff-5335-b104-60a373cf8855@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, June 21\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 40m\n\n1955 | 100 min | UK/USA/Italy | Technicolor
  | English/Italian | Not Rated | 35mm  \nDIRECTED BY: David Lean \nWRITT
 EN BY: H. E. Bates\, David Lean \nWITH: Katharine Hepburn\, Rossano Brazz
 i\, Isa Miranda\, Darren McGavin\nNew print courtesy the Academy Film Arch
 ive.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nRing in the solstice with the smoldering passi
 on of David Lean’s 1955 sumptuous Technicolor romance. Shot on location 
 in Venice\, Italy during the sunniest months of the year\, Summertime feat
 ures Katharine Hepburn as a romantic lead. Hepburn is utterly relatable an
 d captivating in her Oscar-nominated turn as Jane Hudson\, an unmarried se
 cretary on a long-awaited solo vacation away from her humdrum life in Akro
 n\, Ohio. \nFeaturing leisurely footage of the crowded Piazza San Marco an
 d soothing gondola rides along the Fondamenta San Felice\, Lean’s film\,
  for which he received a Directing nomination at the 28th Academy Awards\,
  manifests his understanding of nuanced female interiority through his clo
 seups on Hepburn’s engrossing\, dynamic face. Don’t miss this opportun
 ity to see a gorgeous 35mm print from the Academy Film Archive\; it was st
 ruck in 2004 and has screened no more than three times. \nSummertime was r
 estored in 2003 by the Academy Film Archive and the British Film Institute
  with the support of the David Lean Foundation.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/summertime-019db108-1
 3ff-5335-b104-60a373cf8855
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Phantom Thread in 70mm
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260621
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260622
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019d8808-824f-8193-5719-ea7f79594e16@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, June 21\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 10m\n\n2017 | 130 min. | USA | Color | English | R
 ated R | 70mm\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Paul Thomas Anderson \nWITH: Daniel Da
 y-Lewis\, Lesley Manville\, Vicky Krieps\, Camilla Rutherford\nPrint court
 esy of the Academy Film Archive.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nDaniel Day-Lewis r
 eunited with his There Will Be Blood director Paul Thomas Anderson for thi
 s offbeat romantic drama set in 1950s England. Day-Lewis plays Reynolds Wo
 odcock\, a brilliant clothing designer\, who falls for a young waitress (V
 icky Krieps) only to find their relationship moving in unexpected directio
 ns. Mark Bridges won the Oscar for his elegant costume designs\, and the f
 ilm’s six nominations included Best Picture\, Directing\, and the perfor
 mances of Day-Lewis and Lesley Manville as Woodcock’s strong-willed sist
 er. Radiohead’s Jonny Greenwood\, a regular Anderson collaborator\, rece
 ived his first Oscar nomination for the score. Inspired by the kinds of ar
 tists Day-Lewis’s character would listen to\, such as Nelson Riddle and 
 especially Glenn Gould\, Greenwood composed a score dominated by piano and
  what Anderson called “big-ass strings.”
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/phantom-thread-019d88
 08-824f-8193-5719-ea7f79594e16
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Crash in 4K
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260622
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260623
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd572-68b7-baa0-a568-ca93762acf21@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, June 22\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 40m\n\n1996 | 100 min. | Canada | Color | English 
 | NC-17 | 4K DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: David Cronenberg\nWITH: James Spade
 r\, Holly Hunter\, Elias Koteas\, Deborah Unger\n\nType: Screenings\n\nThe
  “reshaping of the human body by modern technology\,” in the words of 
 one character\, takes center stage in David Cronenberg’s 1996 cult class
 ic Crash\, based on the J. G. Ballard novel of the same name. Film produce
 r James Ballard (James Spader) is drawn into an underground community of c
 ar-crash fetishists after experiencing a near-fatal collision with one of 
 its members. As Ballard and his wife\, Catherine (Deborah Unger)\, grow mo
 re absorbed in this erotic hobby\, they will stop at nothing\, including d
 eath\, to reach their next climax. Highly controversial upon release\, thi
 s cold and clinical exploration of machinery as an extension of the human 
 body\, and how destruction begets creation\, culminates in one of Cronenbe
 rg’s most polarizing films\, and what writer-director Bernardo Bertolucc
 i has described as a “religious masterpiece.”
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/crash-019dd572-68b7-b
 aa0-a568-ca93762acf21
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Pom Poko
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260622
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260623
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd4ea-5df0-6755-75ac-a923956a708e@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, June 22\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 59m\n\n1994 | 119 min. | Japan | Color | Japanese 
 with English subtitles | Rated PG | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Isao Takahat
 a \nWITH: Shincho Kokontei\, Makoto Nonomura\, Yuriko Ishida\, Norihei Mi
 ki\n\nType: Screenings\n\nA motley band of tanuki—shapeshifting wild rac
 coon dogs—must battle humans to protect the idyllic Tama Hills from bein
 g converted into a suburb. Isao Takahata’s epic is a playful and enterta
 ining adventure brimming with visual delights and surprises—the film’s
  nocturnal spirit parade is a showstopper\, with many iconic characters fr
 om other Studio Ghibli films\, including Kiki’s Delivery Service and My 
 Neighbor Totoro\, appearing in the sequence. A huge local hit that remains
  an under-screened gem in the Studio Ghibli catalog\, Pom Poko infuses Jap
 anese mythology with madcap energy\, bringing a light tone to heavy topics
  such as gentrification and deforestation\, as the tanuki call on their co
 mmunity to build a place where people can live in harmony despite their di
 fferences.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/pom-poko-019dd4ea-5df
 0-6755-75ac-a923956a708e
END:VEVENT
