BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Notorious with Guillermo del Toro
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260625
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260626
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dda4c-6058-561e-0943-f275f3a7f670@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Thursday\, June 25\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motio
 n Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 41m\n\n1946 | 101 min. | USA | Black-and-White |
  English | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Alfred Hitchcock \nWRITTEN BY: Ben Hecht 
 \nWITH: Cary Grant\, Ingrid Bergman\, Claude Rains\, Louis Calhern\n\nType
 : Screenings\n\nDirector and lifelong Alfred Hitchcock fan Guillermo del T
 oro delivers an in-depth lecture on this quintessential spy thriller from 
 the Master of Suspense\, followed by a screening. \nThe date of this event
  has moved to June 25. For questions or to request a refund\, email museum
 tickets@oscars.org.\nOne of Hitchcock’s most significant masterpieces ma
 rries a tense post-WWII espionage drama with an intense love story. Cary G
 rant and Ingrid Bergman play charming agent T. R. Devlin and patriotic Ame
 rican Alicia Huberman\, whose father is a convicted Nazi. Helplessly head 
 over heels for Devlin\, Alicia cannot refuse when he asks her to spy on an
 d seduce Alexander Sebastian (Claude Rains)\, a Nazi hiding out in Rio de 
 Janeiro. Elegantly formulated camera movements orchestrated with dense\, e
 motional performances iterate Hitchcock’s incomparable sensibility and m
 astery of the cinematic language of suspense.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/notorious-with-guille
 rmo-del-toro-019dda4c-6058-561e-0943-f275f3a7f670
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Shadow of a Doubt with Guillermo del Toro
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260626
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260627
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dda4f-bd35-37fa-baa8-c9a1d9017b86@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, June 26\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 48m\n\n1943 | 108 min. | USA | Black-and-White | E
 nglish | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Alfred Hitchcock \nWRITTEN BY: Thornton Wil
 der\, Sally Benson\, Alma Reville \nSTORY BY: Gordon McDonell \nWITH: Tere
 sa Wright\, Joseph Cotten\, MacDonald Carey\, Patricia Collinge\n\nType: S
 creenings\n\nDirector and lifelong Alfred Hitchcock fan Guillermo del Toro
  delivers an in-depth lecture on this twisted family portrait from the Mas
 ter of Suspense\, followed by a screening. \nThe date of this event has mo
 ved to June 26. For questions or to request a refund\, email museumtickets
 @oscars.org.\nShadow of a Doubt strikes an intimate noir tone\, and featur
 es Teresa Wright as Charlotte “Young Charlie” Newton\, named after her
  favorite uncle\, Charles Oakley (Joseph Cotton). Set in the warm and invi
 ting town of Santa Rosa\, California\, where a strong sense of communal se
 curity lingers in the air\, this psychological thriller surveys the notion
  of human trust and its fragility through Charlotte’s growing suspicion 
 of her uncle in the notorious Merry Widow murder case. The high-contrast l
 ighting and meticulous application of shadows are woven in the storytellin
 g\, elegantly orchestrated by the boldly framed static shots and dramatic 
 movements of the camera.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/shadow-of-a-doubt-wit
 h-guillermo-del-toro-019dda4f-bd35-37fa-baa8-c9a1d9017b86
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:There's No Business Like Show Business
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260626
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260627
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dda69-eb64-242b-17a3-0f3f59a296b3@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, June 26\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 57m\n\n1954 | 117 min | USA | Color | English | No
 t Rated | DCP\nDIRECTED BY: Walter Lang \nWRITTEN BY: Phoebe Ephron\, Hen
 ry Ephron \nWITH: Ethel Merman\, Donald O'Connor\, Marilyn Monroe\, Dan D
 ailey\n\nType: Screenings\n\nThe Donahue clan\, led by husband and wife Mo
 lly and Terry (Ethel Merman and Dan Dailey)\, navigate the ups and downs o
 f show biz\, from their beginnings in Vaudeville to the Great Depression\,
  in this musical comedy with songs by Irving Berlin. The family’s close 
 bond is further tested with the arrival of the talented and driven Vicky P
 arker (Marilyn Monroe). Costume designer Travilla played an integral role 
 in shaping Marilyn Monroe’s public image on- and off-screen. Together th
 ey famously produced looks that evaded censorship while still courting con
 troversy. His designs for her showgirl characters are of particular note.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/theres-no-business-li
 ke-show-business-019dda69-eb64-242b-17a3-0f3f59a296b3
END:VEVENT
