UID:019e289e-6d6a-02c1-581e-1379f73b67b4@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Conversations
DESCRIPTION:Costume and textile conservator Melinda Kerstein and Icon Coll
 ection Co-Founder Bryan Johns explore the legacy of Marilyn Monroe through
  her iconic onscreen looks.\n\nFriday\, June 26\, 2026 at Noon\n\nLocation
 : Sidney Poitier Grand Lobby\n\nRuntime: 1h\n\nType: Conversations\n\nCost
 ume and textile conservator Melinda Kerstein and Icon Collection Co-Founde
 r Bryan Johns explore the legacy of Marilyn Monroe through her iconic onsc
 reen looks. \nAgainst the backdrop of the largest exhibition of Monroe's o
 nscreen costumes\, the conversation also delves into the late actress’s 
 personal style and the many visual elements that came together to seal her
  place among Hollywood legends. \nAssociate Curator Sophia Serrano moderat
 es.
