DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260627
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260628
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dda63-5be8-c4a8-aa3e-738053c6e3dd@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, June 27\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motio
 n Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 55m\n\n1957 | 115 min | USA | Technicolor | Engl
 ish | Not Rated | 35mm \nDIRECTED BY: Laurence Olivier \nWRITTEN BY: Ter
 ence Rattigan \nWITH: Marilyn Monroe\, Laurence Olivier\, Sybil Thorndike
 \, Richard Wattis\n\nType: Screenings\n\nThe Prince and the Showgirl in 35
 mmIn this sole collaboration between Warner Bros. and Marilyn Monroe Produ
 ctions\, Monroe plays Elsie Marina\, a witty American showgirl who gets no
 ticed by the eccentric Prince Regent Charles (Laurence Olivier). Set in Ed
 wardian London and directed by Olivier\, the film was a famously troubled 
 production\, with tension between co-stars and cinematographer Jack Cardif
 f. The film was shot at Pinewood Studios outside London\; Monroe’s diffi
 culties on and off set were adapted into Simon Curtis’s fictional My Wee
 k with Marilyn (2011)\, with Michelle Williams starring as Monroe.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-prince-and-the-sh
 owgirl-with-bus-stop-019dda63-5be8-c4a8-aa3e-738053c6e3dd
