BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:30th Anniversary of From Dusk Till Dawn with Robert Rodriguez\, pl
 us a performance by Robert Rodriguez's CHINGON BAND
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260718
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260719
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019db1fc-f863-def8-3638-c35bc75970cc@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: Robert Rodriguez\n\nSaturday\, July 18\, 2026\n\nLo
 cation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 48m\n\n1996. 108 
 min. USA. Color. English. Rated R. DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Robert Rodriguez  \
 nWRITTEN BY: Quentin Tarantino \nSTORY BY: Robert Kurtzman \nWITH: Harvey
  Keitel\, George Clooney\, Quentin Tarantino\, Juliette Lewis\n\nType: Scr
 eenings\n\nAfter establishing himself as a cinematic powerhouse with his s
 uccessful indie action film El Mariachi (1992) and its studio-backed seque
 l\, Desperado (1995)\, Robert Rodriguez upped the ante with his next featu
 re\, introducing horror elements to his world of stylish\, neo-western act
 ion films. Violent fugitives the Gecko brothers (portrayed by George Cloon
 ey and the film’s screenwriter\, Quentin Tarantino)\, take a widowed pas
 tor (Harvey Keitel) and his teen children hostage\, hoping to cross the Me
 xican border undetected. Ending up in a saloon full of exotic dancers and 
 rowdy bikers\, the group is confronted by an ancient evil\, spurring an al
 l-night fight for survival. Featuring supporting roles by Cheech Marin\, F
 red Williamson\, and Salma Hayek\, From Dusk Till Dawn is a riotous thrill
  ride packed with gunslinging action and vampire violence that has gone on
  to achieve cult status\, continuing to keep fans partying all night long.
  \nThis program begins with a screening\, followed by a conversation with
  filmmaker Robert Rodriguez and a live performance from his band.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/30th-anniversary-of-f
 rom-dusk-till-dawn-with-robert-rodriguez-019db1fc-f863-def8-3638-c35bc7597
 0cc
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Great Mouse Detective
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260718
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260719
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019db101-4c28-f4d0-d99e-71207761efa6@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, July 18\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motio
 n Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 11m\n\n1986 | 71 min. | USA | Color | English | 
 Rated G | DCP \nDIRECTED BY: John Musker\, Ron Clements\, Dave Michener\, 
 Burny Mattinson \nWRITTEN BY: Pete Young\, Vance Gerry\, Steve Hulett\, R
 on Clements\, John Musker\, Bruce M. Morris\, Matthew O’Callaghan\, Burn
 y Mattinson\, Dave Michener\, Melvin Shaw.  \nWITH: Vincent Price\, Barri
 e Ingham\, Val Bettin\, Alan Young\n\nType: Screenings\n\nA mouse living i
 n the cellar of Sherlock Holmes’s house is himself a brilliant detective
  in this mystery inspired by the Basil of Baker Street books by Eve Titus 
 and Paul Galdone. Four directors collaborated on this charming animated fe
 ature\, including Disney veteran Burny Mattinson and the team of John Musk
 er and Ron Clements (The Little Mermaid\, 1989\, Aladdin\, 1992)\, while V
 incent Price loaned his unmistakable voice to the evil Professor Ratigan. 
 The lighthearted score was composed by four-time Oscar winner Henry Mancin
 i\, his first for an animated feature.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-great-mouse-detec
 tive-019db101-4c28-f4d0-d99e-71207761efa6
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:25th Anniversary of Spy Kids with Robert Rodriguez\, plus a perfor
 mance by The Rodriguez Family SPY BAND
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260720
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019db1ff-c1d7-27a3-7600-c9e6b670fc82@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: Robert Rodriguez\n\nSunday\, July 19\, 2026\n\nLoca
 tion: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 28m\n\n2001. 88 min
 . USA. Color. English. Rated PG. DCP \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Robert Rodrig
 uez \nWITH: Antonio Banderas\, Carla Gugino\, Alexa PenaVega\, Daryl Saba
 ra\n\nType: Screenings\n\nCarmen (Alexa PenaVega) and Juni Cortez (Daryl S
 abara) come from a normal\, boring family. They deal with everyday problem
 s\, such as school bullies and warts\, until they discover their parents\,
  Gregorio (Antonio Banderas) and Ingrid (Carla Gugino)\, are secret agents
  who have been captured by an evil television host\, Fegan Floop (Alan Cum
 ming). Carmen and Juni must overcome their fears and work together to save
  their parents and\, ultimately\, the world. Robert Rodriguez’s Spy Kids
  is an epic kid-power fantasy blending the action of James Bond with the w
 himsy of Willy Wonka in a film that feels straight from the mind of a chil
 d. Filled with fantastical characters\, mutated creatures\, and inventive 
 gadgets\, this enduring children’s classic sparked a vast franchise and 
 was added to the United States National Film Registry in 2024. \nThis pro
 gram begins with a screening\, followed by a conversation with filmmaker R
 obert Rodriguez and a live performance from his band.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/25th-anniversary-of-s
 py-kids-with-robert-rodriguez-019db1ff-c1d7-27a3-7600-c9e6b670fc82
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fantômas Episodes 1-5
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260719
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260720
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd580-a360-5491-7f1f-62166fa72be4@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, July 19\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 5h 20m\n\n1913-14 | 320 min. | France | Black-and-Whi
 te | French | Not Rated | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Louis Feuillade \nWIT
 H: René Navarre\, Edmund Breon\, Georges Melchior\, Renée Carl\n\nType: 
 Screenings\n\nA form most popular in the early 20th century\, a film seria
 l is a story told over a sequence of short episodes\, with each piece inte
 nded to be viewed before a feature-length film. These bite-size programs w
 ere presented weekly in chronological order\, adding entertainment and val
 ue to a program\, and were a common component of the filmgoing experience 
 through the 1940s. A gripping crime thriller showcasing stunning visual co
 mpositions and production design\, Fantômas is a five-part episodic seria
 l based on the novel of the same name by Marcel Allain and Pierre Souvestr
 e. Set in Paris\, the series follows a manhunt by Inspector Juve (Edmund B
 reon) for Fantômas (René Navarre)\, an infamous criminal who is also a m
 aster of disguise\, completely his victims and the authorities.\nThe sched
 ule of breaks will be posted closer to showtime.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/fantomas-e-1-5-019dd5
 80-a360-5491-7f1f-62166fa72be4
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Le Cercle Rouge in 4K
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260720
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260721
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd581-418a-70dd-ff2c-889ba35b3859@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, July 20\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 20m\n\n1970 | 140 min. | France | Color | French |
  Not Rated | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Jean-Pierre Melville \nWRITTEN BY: Jean
 -Pierre Melville \nWITH: Alain Delon\, André Bourvil\, Gian Maria Volont
 è\, Yves Montand\n\nType: Screenings\n\nMaster of French crime thrillers 
 Jean-Pierre Melville landed this gangster epic toward the end of his filmo
 graphy\, before his sudden death at 55. Dense\, atmospheric components of 
 neo noir amplify a stoic persona elegantly delivered by Alain Delon in his
  portrayal of master thief Corey. Along with infamous prison escapee Vogel
  and troubled ex-cop Jansen\, he plans a jewelry heist so risky as to assu
 me the three are doomed\, perhaps even to death. Eventually compassion and
  friendship bloom —the epitome of balance.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/le-cercle-rouge-019dd
 581-418a-70dd-ff2c-889ba35b3859
