BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Spirited Away in 35mm
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260720
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260721
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd515-2d0b-9831-de23-02777c0d6b0c@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, July 20\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion 
 Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 5m\n\n2001 | 125 min. | Japan | Color | Japanese w
 ith English subtitles | Rated PG | 35mm\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Hayao Miyaza
 ki \nWITH: Rumi Hiiragi\, Miyu Irino\, Mari Natsuki\, Takashi Naito \nNew
  subtitled print courtesy of the Academy Film Archive\, with special thank
 s to Studio Ghibli.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nSpirited Away was Hayao Miyazak
 i’s first Oscar win\, and the first hand-drawn\, non-English-language an
 imated film to win the Academy Award for Best Animated Feature. The film i
 nvites audiences into a mind-bending supernatural realm when a wrong turn 
 on a family road trip lands 10-year-old Chihiro in a mysterious dimension 
 populated by all manner of creatures\, including soot gremlins (first intr
 oduced in My Neighbor Totoro)\, the giant witch Yubaba\, and\, most memora
 bly\, the enigmatic No Face. To find her parents and return to the real wo
 rld\, Chihiro must work at an enchanted bathhouse serving spirits of all s
 hapes and sizes. A tour de force of surrealist invention\, Spirited Away i
 s a timeless wonder filled with whimsy and joy.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/spirited-away-019dd51
 5-2d0b-9831-de23-02777c0d6b0c
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Downhill Racer in 35mm
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260722
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260723
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd530-50e1-a2f7-0398-9b2968ece910@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: film editor Richard A. Harris and Academy Governor 
 Jason Reitman \nSelected by the Directors Branch\n\nWednesday\, July 22\, 
 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 41m\n\n
 1969 | 101 min. | USA | Color | English/German/French | Rated PG | 35mm \n
 DIRECTED BY: Michael Ritchie \nWRITTEN BY: James Salter \nWITH: Robert Red
 ford\, Gene Hackman\, Camilla Sparv\, Joe Jay Jalbert \n35mm print courtes
 y of Paramount Pictures Archive.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nRobert Redford use
 d the clout from the success of Butch Cassidy and the Sundance Kid—and h
 is personal obsession with winter sports—to spearhead this character stu
 dy set in the international world of downhill skiing. Redford plays David 
 Chappellet\, a talented athlete for whom relationships are secondary to hi
 s drive to compete. Michael Ritchie made his impressive directorial featur
 e debut with this atypical sports drama\, filming his actors at authentic 
 skiing events. Ritchie’s later three decades demonstrated his aptitude i
 n a wide variety of genres and included classics such as the original The 
 Bad News Bears (1976) and the Oscar-winning political satire The Candidate
  (1972)\, which reunited him with Redford.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/downhill-racer-019dd5
 30-50e1-a2f7-0398-9b2968ece910
END:VEVENT
