BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fatal Attraction with Adrian Lyne
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260813
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260814
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd58c-f37f-8692-e2f3-b2c358295fda@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: director Adrian Lyne\n\nThursday\, August 13\, 2026
 \n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 59m\n\n1987
  | 119 min. | USA | Color | English | Rated R | 4K DCP\nDIRECTED BY: Adria
 n Lyne \nWRITTEN BY: James Dearden \nWITH: Michael Douglas\, Glenn Close
 \, Anne Archer\, Ellen Hamilton Latzen\n\nType: Screenings\n\nAdrian Lyne
 ’s groundbreaking 1987 erotic thriller\, which garnered six Oscar nomina
 tions\, contributed to the phenomenal boom of this subgenre\, and it remai
 ns iconic and timeless. Glenn Close is compelling in her portrayal of Alex
 \, a book editor who has an affair with Dan (Michael Douglas)\, a happily 
 married attorney whose life becomes an unbearable torture after the tryst.
  Passion turns into obsession\; Alex not only terrorizes Dan but also his 
 wife and young daughter. Close’s deep dive into Alex’s psychological s
 tate\, exhibited in the extreme measures she takes to possess Dan\, is man
 ifested in an intense performance\,and the chemistry she shares with Dougl
 as’s riveting Dan creates simultaneously repulsive and magnetic dynamics
  between them.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/fatal-attraction-019d
 d58c-f37f-8692-e2f3-b2c358295fda
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Unfaithful with Adrian Lyne
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd58d-916f-a50b-c633-78a0ffd1e907@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: director Adrian Lyne\n\nFriday\, August 14\, 2026\n
 \nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 4m\n\n2002 | 
 124 min. | USA | Color | English | Rated R | 35mm\nDIRECTED BY: Adrian Lyn
 e \nWRITTEN BY: Alvin Sargent\, William Broyles\, Jr. \nWITH: Diane Lane
 . Richard Gere. Olivier Martinez\, Erik Per Sullivan \nPrint courtesy of t
 he Academy Film Archive.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nDiane Lane received an Osc
 ar nomination for her remarkable portrayal of Connie Sumner\, who lives an
  admirable life in an upper-class neighborhood of upstate New York with lo
 ving husband Edward and 8-year-old son Charlie. In a gush of wind\, an unp
 redictable encounter occurs between Connie and an attractive man in the st
 reet of New York City\, followed by the irreversible measures of an illici
 t affair. Adrian Lyne candidly and without judgment surveys on lust\, pass
 ion\, jealousy\, and guilt\, unearthing a dark\, dense pool of human emoti
 on and the arbitrariness of its motivation.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/unfaithful-019dd58d-9
 16f-a50b-c633-78a0ffd1e907
END:VEVENT
