DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260814
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd51e-9196-b3fe-be48-1f0c289cf9e4@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Friday\, August 14\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motio
 n Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 59m\n\n2004 | 119 min. | Japan | Color | Japanes
 e with English subtitles | Rated PG | DCP\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Hayao Miya
 zaki \nWITH: Chieko Baisho\, Takuya Kimura\, Akihiro Miwa\, Tatsuya Gash
 ûin\n\nType: Screenings\n\nAn adaptation of Diana Wynne Jones’s fantasy
  novel of the same name\, the Oscar-nominated Howl’s Moving Castle is a 
 pitch-perfect fairy tale about aging and war\, set in a dazzling steampunk
  world. When young hatmaker Sophie is transformed into a 90-year-old woman
  by the vengeful Witch of the Waste\, she seeks to break the curse with th
 e help of the enigmatic wizard Howl\, the fire demon Calcifer\, and the ma
 gical moving castle they inhabit.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/howls-moving-castle-0
 19dd51e-9196-b3fe-be48-1f0c289cf9e4
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:The Ugly with Yeon Sang-ho and Park Jeong-min
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019e0a0a-e285-aa70-93a8-d960d2b0c160@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: director Yeon Sang-ho and actor Park Jeong-min\n\nS
 aturday\, August 15\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\
 n\nRuntime: 1h 43m\n\n2025 | 103 min. | Korea | Color | Korean | Rated R |
  DCP \nDIRECTED BY: Yeon Sang-ho \nWRITTEN BY: Yeon Sang-ho.\nWITH: Park 
 Jeong-min\, Kwon Hae-hyo\, Shin Hyun-bin\, Han Ji-hyun\n\nType: Screenings
 \n\nStarring in Yeon Sang-ho’s intimate suspense drama is Park Jeong-min
 \, in his compelling portrayal of Dong-hwan and the younger version of his
  father\, Yeong-gyu\, in flashback sequences. Yeong-gyu\, who cannot see\,
  is a renowned wooden seal carver\, respected for his intricate craftsmans
 hip. Dong-hwan has no memory of his mother\, who has been missing for 40 y
 ears—or so he’s been told—until he receives a startling call about h
 er remains. Adapted from his own graphic novel\, Yeon excavates the ugly a
 spects of societal standards and perceptions of beauty\, and unapologetica
 lly exhibits the dark sides of human greed\, desire\, and trauma.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/the-ugly-019e0a0a-e28
 5-aa70-93a8-d960d2b0c160
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Train to Busan in 4K with Yeon Sang-ho
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019e0a0b-adbd-3b4f-a93e-c94024d83aed@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: director Yeon Sang-ho\n\nSaturday\, August 15\, 202
 6\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 58m\n\n201
 6 | 118 min. | Korea | Color | Korean | Not Rated | 4K DCP \nDIRECTED/WRIT
 TEN BY: Yeon Sang-ho \nWITH: Gong Yoo\, Jung Yu-mi\, Ma Dong-seok\, Kim Su
 -an\n\nType: Screenings\n\nWith the South Korean peninsula in the throes o
 f a national disaster\, travelers board the KTX\, a fast a train to Busan\
 , a city unaffected by the crisis. Among them is Seok-woo\, a workaholic f
 ather traveling with his daughter. When a young woman\, scuffed and dazed\
 , gets on board\, an unimaginable horror erupts in the train’s claustrop
 hobic confines. Director Yeon Sang-ho\, whose prior filmmaking comprises g
 roundbreaking animated features\, balances an upbeat\, kinetic energy with
  solid emotional storytelling to deliver much more than just an action-dri
 ven genre film.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/train-to-busan-019e0a
 0b-adbd-3b4f-a93e-c94024d83aed
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Scooby-Doo in 35mm
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260815
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019db103-7ebb-e23a-c52a-b153e188f713@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, August 15\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Mot
 ion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 26m\n\n2002 | 86 min. | USA | Color | English 
 | Rated PG | 35mm \nDIRECTED BY: Raja Gosnell \nWRITTEN BY: James Gunn 
 \nSTORY BY: Craig Titley\, James Gunn\nWITH: Freddie Prinze Jr.\, Sarah Mi
 chelle Gellar\, Matthew Lillard\, Linda Cardellini\n\nType: Screenings\n\n
 The Mystery Inc. gang from Hanna-Barbera’s classic cartoon\, Scooby-Doo\
 , Where Are You! took their sleuthing skills to the big screen with their 
 first live-action adventure in 2002’s Scooby-Doo. Led by ‘90s teen hea
 rtthrobs and real-life couple Freddie Prinze Jr. and Sarah Michelle Gellar
  as Fred and Daphne\, the amateur detectives Velma (Linda Cardellini)\, Sh
 aggy (Matthew Lillard) and his best friend\, the cowardly\, always hungry\
 , and vocal Great Dane\, Scooby-Doo\, reunite to solve the mystery of ghos
 tly happenings at the tropical resort Spooky Island. From a script co-writ
 ten by James Gunn and featuring Rowan Atkinson as the eccentric resort-own
 er\, the film was a box office success on its release and continues to hav
 e an avid following.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/scooby-doo-019db103-7
 ebb-e23a-c52a-b153e188f713
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Munich in 35mm
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260816
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260817
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019d8804-e004-8e70-0ae5-e53d81175bb7@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Sunday\, August 16\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motio
 n Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 47m\n\n2005 | 167 min. | USA | Color | Scope | E
 nglish/German/French/Hebrew | Rated R | 35mm \nDIRECTED BY: Steven Spielbe
 rg \nWRITTEN BY: Tony Kushner\, Eric Roth \nWITH: Eric Bana\, Daniel Craig
 \, Ciaran Hinds\, Geoffrey Rush\nPrint courtesy of the Academy Film Archiv
 e.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nAfter the killing of Israeli hostages at the 197
 2 Summer Olympics in Munich\, a Mossad agent (Eric Bana) assembles a team 
 to assassinate the men deemed responsible for the murders. Steven Spielber
 g’s fact-based international thriller is a thoughtful look at the moral 
 costs of violence\, with gripping suspense and an impressive supporting ca
 st including Best Actor winner Geoffrey Rush (Shine\, 1996)\, Supporting A
 ctor nominee Ciarán Hinds (Belfast\, 2021)\, and Daniel Craig\, shortly b
 efore he debuted as James Bond. The film received five Oscar nominations i
 ncluding Best Picture\, Directing\, and\, for John Williams’ music\, his
  22nd feature score for the director. Williams’s somber\, restrained sco
 re focused on\, in the composer’s words\, “the enormous suffering and 
 guilt\, and eventually\, paranoia” of Bana’s protagonist.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/munich-019d8804-e004-
 8e70-0ae5-e53d81175bb7
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Snake of June
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260817
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260818
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd58f-be6b-74f3-d4b0-11084892d642@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, August 17\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motio
 n Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 17m\n\n2002 | 77 min. | Japan | Color | Japanese
  with English subtitles | Rated R | DCP \nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Shinya Tsu
 kamoto \nWITH: Asuka Kurosawa\, Yuji Kotari\, Shinya Tsukamoto\, Susumu T
 erajima\n\nType: Screenings\n\nRinko Tatsumi (Asuka Kurosawa) is a suicide
  hotline worker resigned to a life of unhappiness until she receives a pac
 kage from a blackmailer. Through the increasingly vulgar acts of exhibitio
 nism her blackmailer forces upon her\, she learns to shed the social restr
 ictions and repression dominating her life. Shot on black-and-white film a
 nd tinted a monochromatic blue\, Shinya Tsukamoto’s A Snake of June is a
  visual feast. Filled with shaky\, hand-held camerawork\, voyeuristic clos
 e-ups\, and near-constant rain\, Tsukamoto creates a damp and cold erotic 
 thriller that explores sexual dynamics\, transformation\, and releasing on
 e's inner desires.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/a-snake-of-june-019dd
 58f-be6b-74f3-d4b0-11084892d642
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ponyo in 35mm
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260817
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260818
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd51f-43b5-e687-8774-0d5f81c04a9c@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:Monday\, August 17\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum of Motio
 n Pictures\n\nRuntime: 1h 43m\n\n2008 | 103 min. | Japan | Color | Japanes
 e with English subtitles| Rated G | 35mm\nDIRECTED/WRITTEN BY: Hayao Miyaz
 aki \nWITH: Tomoko Yamaguchi\, Kazushige Nagashima\, Yuki Amami\, George 
 Tokoro \nNew subtitled print courtesy of the Academy Film Archive\, with 
 special thanks to Studio Ghibli.\n\nType: Screenings\n\nPonyo focuses on t
 he friendship between 5-year-old Sosuke and a magical goldfish named Brunh
 ilde\, the young daughter of a sorcerer father and a sea-goddess mother. A
 fter wandering away from her father’s four-flippered submarine\, Brunhil
 de washes ashore and is discovered by the curious Sosuke. Now renamed Pony
 o\, she forms a quick bond with Sosuke that fuels her yearning to be a rea
 l girl\, and together they shoulder the cost of what that might take. The 
 vibrant and colorful hand-drawn animations are a delight for audiences of 
 all ages\, as Hayao Miyazaki builds a world filled with magical goldfish\,
  spellcasters\, and sea goddesses in this tale of how friendships can blos
 som anywhere—even in the ocean’s depths.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/ponyo-019dd51f-43b5-e
 687-8774-0d5f81c04a9c
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Out of Sight
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260819
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260820
DTSTAMP:20260614T091037Z
UID:019dd532-0b98-b1eb-af29-bc9f09d740b6@academymuseum.org
CATEGORIES:Screenings
DESCRIPTION:In person: film editors Robb Sullivan\, John Axelrad and Emma 
 E. Hickox\, and Academy Governor Stephen Rivkin. \nSelected by the Film Ed
 itors Branch\n\nWednesday\, August 19\, 2026\n\nLocation: Academy Museum o
 f Motion Pictures\n\nRuntime: 2h 3m\n\n1998 | 123 min. | USA | Color | Eng
 lish | Rated R | DCP\nDIRECTED BY: Steven Soderbergh \nWRITTEN BY: Scott F
 rank \nWITH: George Clooney\, Jennifer Lopez\, Ving Rhames\, Don Cheadle\n
 \nType: Screenings\n\nBank robber Jake Foley’s prison escape is complica
 ted by an inconvenient encounter with U.S. marshal Karen Sisco\, and an un
 expected attraction between them. Making his first major studio film\, dir
 ector Steven Soderbergh\, working with an Oscar nominated screenplay by Sc
 ott Frank\, brings the world of master crime novelist Elmore Leonard to th
 e screen in a dazzling combination of old-fashioned Hollywood glamour and 
 contemporary grit. The film was also nominated for its editing\, by the ac
 complished Anne V. Coates (Lawrence of Arabia\, 1962)\, who employs interc
 utting\, flashbacks\, and freeze frames to enhance the swooningly romantic
  chemistry of stars George Clooney and Jennifer Lopez.
LOCATION:Academy Museum of Motion Pictures
URL:https://www.academymuseum.org/en/programs/detail/out-of-sight-019dd532
 -0b98-b1eb-af29-bc9f09d740b6
END:VEVENT
